Release toolchains bundle third-party programs and libraries for linking (lib/velt/,
lib/targets/; docs/internals/linking.md):

  lib/velt/lld (lld.exe) is LLVM's linker, built from the LLVM project's sources
  (https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project). Copyright (c) the LLVM project contributors. Licensed
  under the Apache License 2.0 with LLVM Exceptions; the full text, with the notices of the
  third-party code LLVM includes, is lib/velt/LICENSE.txt (crates/velt_link/kit/licenses/
  LLVM-LICENSE.txt in the repository). The libunwind.a in the musl link kits
  (lib/targets/*-linux-musl/) is LLVM's libunwind under the same license, as shipped with the
  Rust toolchain.

  The musl link kits (lib/targets/*-linux-musl/: crt1.o, crti.o, crtn.o, crtbegin.o,
  crtend.o, libc.a) are musl libc (https://musl.libc.org) as shipped with the Rust toolchain.
  Copyright (c) 2005-2020 Rich Felker, et al. Licensed under the MIT license; the full text and
  the notices of the code musl includes are lib/targets/*-linux-musl/COPYRIGHT
  (crates/velt_link/kit/licenses/musl-COPYRIGHT.txt in the repository).

  The other link kits are written by Velt: Windows import libraries generated from lists of the
  system DLLs' exported names, Linux stub libraries generated from lists of glibc's exported
  symbol names and versions, and macOS .tbd stubs listing the system libraries' exported symbol
  names. They contain no code from Microsoft, the GNU C Library or Apple.
